commit 0a40342d83ce3e1ea360e27d7131d54d6afcb5b6
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun Jul 5 11:19:23 2026 -0400

    Retire unsent ranges with one batch finalize call
    
      The submit-error paths in submit_upload_ranges and
      submit_download_ranges synthesised failures for never-submitted
      ranges by calling parallel_unit_tracker_finalize in a loop.  Safe,
      but only because the loop count was arithmetically exact: the
      tracker frees itself when remaining hits 0, so the freeing call had
      to be provably the loop's last iteration - an invariant that lived
      in a comment, that scan-build flagged as a potential use-after-free,
      and that any future accounting change would silently break. This is
      an unsual situation but needs to be addressed.
    
      Add parallel_unit_tracker_finalize_n(), which retires n ranges in
      one decrement under one lock acquisition; the existing finalize
      becomes its n=1 wrapper, so the per-range call sites are unchanged.
      The error paths now make a single batch call after which the tracker
      pointer is dead unconditionally - nothing left to get wrong.

