commit a78da1a38f60a2675ceec28f3bc060524ef9ea16
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sat Jul 4 20:21:01 2026 -0400

    Remove experimental TCPRcvBufRescue option.
    
    Testing showed that it was not meeting the requirements for
    improving performance in a high bdp high loss environment. It actually
    reduced perfromance because the window was clamped ot 16MB. Increasing it
    beyond that may have helped *but* it would have been extra complication in an
    attempt to get to where the default code path already was.
    
    This was oringally designed to deal with pathological poor performance
    caused by a TCP window never opening up. The idea was to force it open.
    I know this can happen but addressing this is overly complex.
    The juice isn't worth the squeeze.

