commit f50895031544919b294ef7a7e045368ca4768896
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri Jul 3 23:19:39 2026 -0400

    Make MT-AES-CTR thread/queue counts compile-time constants
    
      Testing on loopback (the maximum-throughput regime - a networked path
      can only be slower) showed one keystream producer thread already keeps
      the queues full at any rate ssh can reach, so the SSH_CIPHER_THREADS
      runtime override bought nothing. Fix the counts at compile time and
      drop the machinery:
    
      SSH_CIPHER_THREADS and NUMKQ (= threads + 1) become #defines; remove
      get_thread_count() (provider path) and the inline getenv (legacy
      path), plus the runtime clamps.
    
      Size the cipher context's per-thread and per-queue arrays by those
      constants instead of MAX_THREADS/MAX_NUMKQ. Only the 2 queues actually
      used are now allocated instead of 33, shrinking each cipher context
      from ~16.5 MB to ~1.0 MB.
    
      Applied to both the OpenSSL-3 provider (cipher-ctr-mt-functions.c/.h)
      and the legacy (cipher-ctr-mt.c) paths.
    
      Tested and no difference in performance.

