commit 3734bb5ae63b827fa21f4038c93ae0c0491a5105
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Mon Jun 29 23:43:56 2026 -0400

    Pass HPN sftp-server toggles via argv instead of the environment
    
      HPNUseBundle and HPNWriterPool were propagated from sshd to the
      hpnsftp-server through the HPN_USE_BUNDLE / HPN_WRITER_POOL environment
      variables. Under PermitUserEnvironment a user could set those names in
      ~/.ssh/environment and override the operator's sshd_config policy.
    
      Convert both toggles to argv flags, mirroring -W.
      -B and -O default on

commit ecfc7c9089d1ec1a7de8dd66c3696a6d064529e0
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Mon Jun 29 22:36:21 2026 -0400

    Fix unsafe scp->hpnscp command rewrite in client
    
      The HPN scp-prefix rewrite used an unchecked malloc(len+4) and
      sprintf("%s", sshbuf_ptr(cmd)), which assumes the sshbuf is
      NUL-terminated at len. sshbuf gives no such guarantee (it only worked
      because recallocarray zeroes slack), so a command that exactly fills
      the allocation could over-read past the buffer. The starts-with-scp
      test also used pos - new_cmd == 0, which is undefined when strstr
      returns NULL. Triggered via the peer's version banner
      (SSH_HPNSSH_PREFIX).
    
      Use sshbuf_dup_string (NUL-terminated, NULL on embedded-NUL/OOM),
      strncmp for the prefix test, and xasprintf for a checked allocation.

