commit e52731da1a2ceb17b0b7dd7037385021eda99544
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun Jun 28 22:04:04 2026 -0400

    sftp parallel: resolve the real Lustre default stripe, drop the 1 MiB guess
    
      compute_range_split's no-stripe fallback hardcoded a 1 MiB alignment as a
      stand-in for "the Lustre default is probably 1 MiB", applied to every
      filesystem with no reported geometry. The root cause was that
      lustre_get_stripe returned 0 for default-striped files (lmm_stripe_size
      == 0 means "inherit the filesystem default"), so the client never saw a
      real stripe on Lustre.
    
      Server (sftp-lustre.c): split the layout-EA parse into read_lov_layout(),
      then have lustre_get_stripe walk up ancestor directories reading each
      default layout (getxattr "lustre.lov", no fork/llapi) until a concrete
      geometry is found - the mount root always carries one. Lustre
      default-striped files now report a real stripe.
    
      Client (sftp-parallel-unit.c): with the default resolved server-side, a
      zero stripe reliably means a non-striped filesystem, so the no-stripe
      path uses plain per_range instead of the 1 MiB guess.

