commit 4e303fd6b4c61e7aa090c5ded1ddd1d984da8b9b
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun Jun 28 20:42:00 2026 -0400

    Fix five code-review findings (memory safety, data integrity, concurrency)
    
      - sftp-hpn-tar.c: reject a bundle entry size > SIZE_MAX before the (size_t)
        malloc, closing a 32-bit truncation -> heap overflow from untrusted input.
      - sftp-hpn-bundle-client.c: on a failed bundle download, reset all entry
        results so the worker re-queues the batch; the pool path marked entries
        done at enqueue, so a deferred writer failure could finalize an unwritten
        file as success (silent data loss; upload/download parity).
      - cipher-chachapoly-libcrypto-mt.c: NULL the EVP_MAC handle after freeing it
        to prevent a double-free on the rekey alloc-failure path.
      - session.c: append -W to the sftp subsystem only when a worker cap is
        configured, so a stock/non-HPN sftp-server keeps working by default.
      - cipher-ctr-mt-functions.c, cipher-ctr-mt.c: mutex-guard the global evp_ptrs
        uthash; pregen threads raced HASH_ADD when SSH_CIPHER_THREADS>1.

