commit 09d97b469bcb4da68df5f21ad6f36a02e764a969
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri Jun 26 21:40:15 2026 -0400

    metrics: serialize modern FreeBSD/OpenBSD tcp_info fields
    
      Bring the BSD serialization path up to current FreeBSD/OpenBSD kernels.
      Adds FreeBSD telemetry (delivered_ce, received_ce, total_tlp,
      total_tlp_bytes, rcv_numsacks, dupacks) and OpenBSD extras (max_sndwnd,
      rttmin, rcv_adv, ts_recent, rfbuf_cnt, rfbuf_ts, and the so_rcv_sb_* /
      so_snd_sb_* socket-buffer block).
    
      BSD has no LINUX_VERSION_CODE equivalent and the FreeBSD/OpenBSD structs
      diverge, so each field is gated by its own autoconf member check
      (HAVE_STRUCT_TCP_INFO_TCPI_*) for compile-time existence plus the runtime
      TCPI_FIELD_IN length gate. The writer block is #ifndef __linux__ so the
      delivered_ce/received_ce counters, which also exist on Linux, are not
      double-emitted there.
    
      delivered_ce and received_ce are shared between Linux and FreeBSD but
      grouped differently per stack, so the reader and header now check those
      two keys per-key instead of by group sentinel. Linux CSV output is
      unchanged (same columns, same order); the BSD-only fields are appended
      per-key.
    
      configure.ac gains the member checks; regenerate configure with
      autoreconf.

