commit 95c072b840962c5c7206b0c03545ddec87f5fcef
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Mon Jun 22 13:14:41 2026 -0400

      Remove the legacy scp (-O) verified-resume path; Remove the legacy scp (-O) verified-resume path
    
      The MODE_SCP resume support (-Z over the legacy rcp protocol) was slow,
      fragile, and is superseded by SFTP-protocol verified resume. Excise it
      from source()/sink(): the R-record resume handshake, the per-file
      remote-hash exchange, the conditional open/lseek, and the shared
      calculate_hash()/HASH_* helpers and xxhash include. -Z now requires SFTP
      mode and is rejected when combined with -O.
    
      Auto-repair was only reachable through the orchestrator's range
      verify. A fresh putv/getv of a smaller file that landed corrupt
      was detected but never repaired: both whole-file verify paths -
      the classic single-conn phase and the orchestrator's parallel_verify_one -
      recorded the mismatch and exited 57 without re-transmitting.
    
      Extract the verify+repair logic into one routine, sftp_hpn_verify_repair(),
      and call it from both whole-file paths so they can no longer drift. On a
      mismatch it repairs at the transfer's own granularity: files >= the
      128 MiB chunk-hash floor splice only the mismatched 64 MiB chunks in place
      (offset-addressed WRITE, no truncation) via the existing chunked
      reconciliation; smaller files re-transmit [0,size) whole. Bounded by the
      attempt cap with convergence (two identical failed dest hashes =
      deterministic fault, bail), matching the orchestrator's range-repair
      policy.
    
      sftp_hpn_verify_transfer() gains a dest-hash out-param for the convergence
      baseline. The repair enable/cap resolution (-X VerifyRepair /
      HPN_NO_VERIFY_REPAIR / HPN_VERIFY_REPAIR_ATTEMPTS) is factored into
      sftp_hpn_verify_repair_resolve(), shared by the orchestrator and the new
      conn-side settings.
    
      Client-side only; no wire change.

