      flag for what -o HPNVerifyTransfer=yes does via ssh_config. We need to remove
      that from ssh_config. It doesn't belong there as an ssh opt.
    
      Byte-granular verify progress meter (server + both clients): the server
      emits hash progress every 1s (HPN_HASH_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SEC) on both the
      sftp-hash-range and hpn-check-file paths; the client drives the meter from
      bytes hashed (per-conn in-flight + per-phase done-bytes, summed across
      workers) instead of a file-count fraction. A single huge file's bar now
      advances every second with a real rate instead of sitting at 0%/stalled
      then jumping to 100%.

