commit 40061816f168db979d8500baf76b458461d5e776
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jun 17 18:44:40 2026 -0400

    That change to O_TRUNC worked.
    
      The durable fix makes the stale write harmless instead of racing it: open
      the extracted file WITHOUT O_TRUNC and set the authoritative size with
      ftruncate() at entry completion - a point only a writer that finished the
      entry reaches. A never-completed partial can then only overwrite a prefix
      with identical bytes and can never shrink the file. Cost-neutral (swaps an
      open-time truncate for a close-time one; no temp+rename, no extra metadata
      op). This resolves a serious problem with silent data corruption.
    
      Removed all of the failed attenpts and the testing infrastructure. Also removed
      a dead function left over from a refactoring.

