commit 3bab5ab9ea707c13a15dbe54545627ea25a2e0bb
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 16:10:02 2026 -0400

    sftp: add HPN_MIDSTREAM_SUB mid-transfer worker substitution (default off)
    
      Experimental, gated behind HPN_MIDSTREAM_SUB (default off). When a worker's
      byte-rate EMA sits below 15% of the fleet median for a few reporter ticks,
      the orchestrator benches that worker and yields its remaining range to a
      healthy peer, so a persistently slow stream stops holding up the transfer.
      Detection is byte-rate only, deliberately avoiding any TCP_INFO channel
      across the key-bearing worker child boundary. A warmup guard on the
      detector, re-armed when a benched worker re-enters the pool, keeps it from
      re-benching on a cold or stale EMA.
    
      Also adds an HPN_BUNDLE_TIMING-gated YIELD-HANDOFF trace that records when a
      yielded range is picked up by a different worker (covers tail-redistribute
      as well as this path).
    
      Evaluation is inconclusive: a clear benefit shows up only when a degraded
      leg is forced into the writing set with no healthy reserves and the test
      path is otherwise clean; with reserves present the slow worker is sidelined
      by the writer cap before this fires, and on a healthy network it neither
      helps nor measurably hurts. Committed default-off as a checkpoint.
    
      We *MUST* verify this and make a decision. Held here only so we don't
      lose the work.

