commit 533563603f91b5dc7279a19b76f3a38e698769fe
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun Jun 14 17:36:40 2026 -0400

    sftp: gate the endgame split to real tails and stagger its launches
    
      Gate maybe_endgame_split on total > writer_cap. When a file has no more
      ranges than the per-inode writer cap, every range starts at once and
      there is no tail to drain; firing the split there only re-injects a
      synchronized writer burst (measured inflating path RTT ~2.5x) and made
      short transfers a net loss. Drop the now-redundant maturity gate - the
      queue-empty condition already implies it on a real tail.
    
      Space the split's N piece submissions by a fixed gap
      (HPN_ENDGAME_SPLIT_STAGGER_MS, default 25 ms) instead of launching them
      simultaneously. The simultaneous launch was a synchronized multi-stream
      burst that spiked path RTT and tripped cwnd-collapse wedges; staggering
      de-correlates the ramps. Set to 0 to restore the old behavior.

