      refresh shows 100% instead of the last reporter tick's stale value.

commit d30f9657ad11e470fbacfe6e675d05d7862bf1e6
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 16:44:51 2026 -0400

    Create range-split destination files lazily at first write
    
      Pre-creating every file full-size at submit left interrupted transfers
      strewn with sparse full-size placeholders: ls showed ten "complete"
      files when eight held no data, and verified resume hashed all of them.
      Create the file at the first dispatched range instead (exactly-once
      via the tracker mutex; create-if-absent so layout-created files and
      existing partials are never touched), pin no size, and let files grow
      to their pwrite highwater - interrupted transfers now show only files
      holding data, at honest sizes.
    
      The full-size pin was also what forced resume onto the chunked path,
      so drop the size-equality gate in both resume dispatches: chunked
      verify engages for any partial when the server supports hash-range
      (short files chunk-clamp and re-send; interior holes refill), with
      prefix resume as the fallback for sequential partials. Fail fast on
      unusable destinations with a directory stat at submit, and classify
      permission-class create failures (EACCES/EROFS/EDQUOT/ENOSPC) as
      permanent so units give up instead of retrying.

