commit 5241d0ad68dc0922c08100c90aa377ab1516d59a
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 10:40:51 2026 -0400

    Measure watchdog silence from lease end, not from the last byte before it
    
      The silence clock kept counting underneath an active watchdog-pause
      lease: a verify that hashes for minutes carried that entire quiet
      phase as accrued silence, so the instant the lease ended (the hash
      helpers resume promptly), one slow first write-ack put the worker
      minutes past the endgame threshold and it was reaped - restarting
      the whole verification from scratch (~3x wall clock, or livelock).
      Re-seed last_progress_ns on every paused tick so a held lease counts
      as progress and post-lease silence is measured from lease end.
    
      I still need to remove the setenv created for testing. I'll do that
      on the next commit as I want to leave that infrastructure in place
      for this.

