commit cbab990f3736c22d379596243f5ff1417ba639be
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 08:40:55 2026 -0400

    Carry hash progress in verify heartbeats so a stalled backend cannot hang the client
    
      Heartbeats prove liveness, not progress: a server alive but making no
      headway (stalled backend) renewed the client's watchdog lease forever
      and a verify would wait eternally. Both hash heartbeats (sftp-hash-range,
      hpn-check-file) now carry a u64 bytes-hashed-so-far figure; a client
      seeing no advance for 120 seconds treats the connection as failed via
      sftp_conn_die() - the operation cannot be abandoned on a live connection
      without desyncing it - and the existing unit-retry machinery takes over.
    
      Includes a temporary HPN_VERIFY_STALL_SEC threshold override for
      testing, tagged for removal before release.

commit b57d5aa2bebe016e14e3f66dc079403ce692a423
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 08:08:08 2026 -0400

    Overhaul interrupt handling and watchdog liveness for parallel transfers
    
      Rebuild the worker fleet on the next command after a SIGINT instead of
      leaving the orchestrator dead. This is acually faster than letting the
      channles drain and reseting the existing connections. Especially if the
      user's reason was because the transfer seemed wedged.
    
      Make teardown deterministic: kill in-flight spawns and worker ssh
      children at abort, escalating to SIGKILL at stop, and drain the queue
      so units and trackers are freed. If we don't do this we can get hangs
      at exit.
    
      Refresh the watchdog pause through long local hash phases so verified
      resume is not reaped mid-hash. This is annoying because it cause the
      verification process to start over from the beginning. This commit
      doesn't fully resolve that. That will be the next commit but I needed
      to get this committed before it got too unwieldy.
    
      The rest is UX and message spam reuction. Carry reaped workers'
      counters into the aggregates so reports survive respawns. Report
      interrupt fallout as one calm resumable-partials summary instead of
      error theater; reduce worker-death output to a single plain-language
      heartbeat per event, with routine churn and transport telemetry at debug.
      Clamp progress-meter rate math against backward steps and
      sub-millisecond refresh windows (the counter can wrap otherwise).

commit f3857f1e332292ab5920ae499a438cdf453f289c
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jun 10 11:12:30 2026 -0400

      Apply Lustre layout to local destinations on download
    
      Uploads set a tiered/plain default layout on the remote destination
      directory via the hpn-file-layout extension; downloads inherited the
      local directory default, typically unstriped. Add a local twin of the
      layout hook with the same HPNLustreStripeCount policy, applied
      directly since the client is the writer - no wire round trip - called
      from the download walker's mkdir and the direct-get path. Link
      sftp-lustre.o into the client binaries. Non-Lustre destinations skip
      silently.

