commit d7a50714b476a14b865e02d29cb9fbbd24cea965
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sat Jun 6 15:10:08 2026 -0400

    sftp-hpn: tiered Lustre auto-layout (stripe-1 small + stripe-N large), no MDT
    
      The default auto-layout (HPNLustreStripeCount unset) previously requested a
      Data-on-MDT composite: small files on the MDT, large files striped across
      n_workers OSTs. This breaks policy at PSC and might at a lot of other places
      as well. So we replace the MDT first component with a single-OST component
      (stripe_count=1, offset -1 round-robin), so small files get one clean OST
      object with no over-striping and NO data on the MDS; large files still stripe
      across n_workers in the overflow component.
    
      Also:
      - Fix the auto-layout guard.  The plain-stripe skip used ">=", which silently
        dropped any request to NARROW a wider inherited default (an explicit
        HPNLustreStripeCount=1 was a no-op on a stripe-8-default dir).  Use "==":
        the explicit count is now authoritative in both directions.
      - Derive the small/large threshold from the filesystem's actual OST stripe
        size (info.stripe_size) instead of a hardcoded 1 MiB; the 1 MiB constant is
        now only a fallback for when the server reports no size.
      - Rename dom_size -> small_threshold across the hpn-file-layout wire (same
        rev-2 u32, back-compatible), use_dom -> use_tiered, and the "Data-on-MDT"
        log/labels -> "tiered composite".
    
      The MDT-backed composite is recoverable from commit 6e585150c.

commit 6e585150c4e2cd733c67fa6c4eb07c6ef1b08bc8
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri Jun 5 14:43:03 2026 -0400

    sftp-hpn-server: set DoM composite layout via fsetxattr, not ioctl
    
      LL_IOC_LOV_SETSTRIPE only accepts simple layouts - it returns ENOTSUPP (524)
      for a composite (COMP_V1) buffer, so the DoM auto-layout silently failed and
      fell back to plain stripe. Set the directory default composite by writing the
      raw lustre.lov EA (mirror of the getxattr read): fsetxattr on the O_RDONLY
      dir fd. Also lcme_id 0 (kernel-assigned) and DoM stripe_offset -1 to match the
      lfs template, and fall back to plain stripe on any DoM failure (not just
      NOT_FS). Verified standalone on br008: a file inherits lmm_pattern: mdt

commit f626162e2a8ffa2f113853d92a7364526585478d
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri Jun 5 14:23:53 2026 -0400

    sftp-hpn: Data-on-MDT auto-layout for small files; shell-free layout path
    
      Auto layout now requests a Data-on-MDT composite (small files on the MDT,
      no per-file OST object - the dominant small-file Lustre create cost) instead
      of striping every file across -j OSTs. Built as a raw
      LL_IOC_LOV_SETSTRIPE composite buffer because we can't count on the remote
      giving us shell access to run things liek getstripe or setstripe. If DoM is
      off/unsupported falls back to a plain stripe. Also convert the layout read
      from fork+exec("lfs getstripe") to getxattr("lustre.lov"), so the whole
      layout path (statfs detect / getxattr read / ioctl set) is shell-free.
      hpn-file-layout wire bumped to rev 2 (dom_size request, layout_kind reply).

commit ee01eec4756b7cf7111bf3d37e35ee95ff201ea9
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri Jun 5 13:23:19 2026 -0400

    sftp-parallel: scale work-queue depth to bundle target; relax silence reaps
    
      Work-queue depth: the depth was N*UPLOAD_BATCH_SIZE*4 - the old 64-file
      pipelining sizing, never updated for byte-capped bundles. Add work_queue_depth():
      in bundle mode size for num_streams full bundles of a representative small
      file plus headroom, capped at WORK_QUEUE_DEPTH_MAX; non-bundle path unchanged.
      Bundles now fill to target. Thsi is important for small files to minimize
      overhead.
    
      Per-worker silence reaps: the orchestrator's mid-stream silence kills (dead
      120s / isolation 15s / iso_stall 60s) pre-empted the transport's peer-stall
      wait+brake, re-manufacturing churn. Raise them to one backstop,
      WORKER_SILENCE_BRAKE_SEC (330s, above the 300s transport brake), so the
      transport self-terminates first and the orchestrator only reaps a still-
      connected silent worker it can't classify. Born-dead stays fast.

