commit 072a088c15dcf87bf9c9818462d4eaace14d86f4
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jun 3 21:24:48 2026 -0400

    sftp-parallel: escalating best-effort respawn cooldown; consolidate monotonic time helpers
    
      1. Respawn cooldown rework (reporter_dispatch_respawns). Replace the
         count-capped, abort-on-exhaust cooldown with an escalating, decaying,
         best-effort back-off.
           - Systemic peer-stall trigger: a rolling ~10-tick window of per-tick
             peer-stall worker deaths; >= max(2, 50% of num_streams) means the
             backend is saturated fleet-wide -> enter/escalate a cooldown. The
             epoch ceiling stays as a cause-agnostic backstop.
           - Escalating duration: base 30s, x2 per burst, cap 3600s; decays /2
             per 30s of sustained healthy throughput and ends an active pause
             early on recovery. Pauses RESPAWNS ONLY; live workers untouched.
           - No count-cap abort: under a transient stall we back off and retry
             indefinitely. Only auto-abort left is a genuine dead-end (all
             workers gone, units pending, not in cooldown, and a respawn could
             not even be launched).
           - Single-probe refill when the fleet is empty (one worker, not
             num_streams) so we don't slam a maybe-still-saturated backend.
    
      2. Consolidate monotonic clock helpers onto misc.c. Add monotime_ns();
         delete the four hand-rolled readers.

commit 47aea49a801a98826ab7f5bc3252b07956a642ed
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jun 3 20:48:49 2026 -0400

    Add LIFO queue insertion for hardfailures.
    
    When a work unit is lost during transit due to a worker exiting or
    dying the work unit is put back at the head of the FIFO work queue. The
    idea is to keep file completion somewhat linear. Fails that are ambiguous
    might be due to non-transient failures which means dropping that unit
    at the front might trigger that failure again quickly. This can
    happen with lustre. The byte range is a continuation of the existent
    file and may land on the same OST again causing rapid churning.

commit b141fdcea1bd0a26fee29f868846a567b6e24c6c
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jun 3 17:06:45 2026 -0400

    sftp-parallel: stop dropping data on transient peer-stall churn
    
      Two parallel-transfer fixes, both client-side in sftp-parallel.c:
    
      1. Don't charge a retry on transient connection death. worker_process_
         result and worker_finalize_one_entry now skip ++u->attempt when
         sftp_conn_is_dead() (wedge / peer-stall / transport drop): the worker
         is about to exit and respawn, so the unit re-queues without burning
         its MAX_RETRIES budget. Only failures on a still-live connection
         (ambiguous server error) charge the budget. Fixes the br008 j8 case
         where peer-stall churn exhausted the retry budget and abandoned a
         file's byte-ranges (~10 GiB lost across 5/20 transfers).
    
      2. Leave failed range partials in place, resumable. range_tracker_
         finalize no longer unlinks/sftp_rm's a partially-failed range file;
         it reports the file as incomplete and leaves it for verified resume
         (reputv / regetv), which refills only the mismatched ranges instead
         of discarding the data that did transfer. Header doc + invariants
         updated to match.

