    sftp-parallel: enforce strict bundle cap + advertise server max
    
      Server advertises HPNMaxBundleSize via the new
      hpn-bundle-max-size@hpnssh.org extension in SSH_FXP_VERSION.  Client
      parses the value into sftp_hpn_conn->server_max_bundle_size and the
      worker init clamps w->bundle_target_bytes to it before bundle mode
      goes live — clients never generate a bundle the server would reject.
    
      Existing server-side bundle_per_cap enforcement remains as belt-and-
      suspenders against old/misbehaving clients.
    
      Fixed a fencepost in the walker's batch loop: gate was
      `batch_bytes <= cap`, so when batch_bytes already equalled cap we
      still popped one more unit only to discover it didn't fit, then
      shoved it through the slow per-file leftover path.

