commit 5df7e2a4c4015daf781b709990d7e8dc077326a2
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun May 31 16:25:43 2026 -0400

     hpn-bundle: operator controls, raise defaults, file-eligibility threshold
    
      Add server-side operator controls for the SFTP bundle path and a
      matching client-side CLI flag.  Raise the default bundle target after
      the libarchive removal decoupled server memory from bundle size.
    
      Client side
      -----------
      * BUNDLE_TARGET_BYTES_DEFAULT raised 4 MiB → 8 MiB (ssh_config default
        raised in lockstep).
      * HPNBundleSize legal range tightened from [64 KiB, 64 MiB] to
        [1 MiB, 64 MiB].  Sub-MiB bundles can't usefully amortise the
        OPEN/CLOSE round-trip cost the eligibility threshold imposes.
      * New hpnsftp CLI flag: --bundle-size N[KMG].  Same clamping as
        HPNBundleSize.
      * New bundle file-size threshold: a unit is marked bundle_ineligible
        in submit() when its size exceeds bundle_target /
        BUNDLE_MIN_FILES_PER_BUNDLE (4 by default — at least 4 files per
        bundle for the OPEN/CLOSE round-trips to amortise).
    
      Server side (sshd_config)
      -------------------------
      * HPNUseBundle yes|no — master toggle.  When no, sftp-server omits
        hpn-bundle / hpn-bundle-fetch from SSH_FXP_VERSION and refuses
        bundle ops with SSH2_FX_OP_UNSUPPORTED (belt-and-suspenders).
      * HPNBundleSize <bytes> — server's preferred default (informational
        today; reserved for future EXT_INFO advertisement so clients can
        clamp proactively).  Range [1 MiB, 64 MiB].
      * HPNMaxBundleSize <bytes> — hard server-side ceiling, overrides the
        existing -B CLI default if -B was not explicitly given.  Range
        [1 MiB, 64 MiB].  Clamp-on-overshoot with one INFO log line per
        session.
      * HPNMaxConcurrentWorkers <N> — parser + sshd -T dump only in this
        commit; cross-process per-user channel-count enforcement deferred
        to a follow-up (needs the counter-file design).

