commit 230cb006cd8b83ace1e054fbf4b9973ad83101fa
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri May 29 16:56:48 2026 -0400

    "sftp: hpn-file-layout extension — Lustre auto-stripe (experimental)
    
      Adds the hpn-file-layout@hpnssh.org SFTP extension and the
      HPNLustreStripeCount ssh_config option (default: auto).  When parallel
      mode is engaged (-j N with N >= 2) and the destination directory is on
      Lustre with stripe_count < N, the orchestrator asks the server to bump
      the directory's stripe via LL_IOC_LOV_SETSTRIPE before any files land
      there.  Subsequent files (range-split slices, bundle-extracted files)
      inherit the wider layout, so workers fan out across multiple OSTs
      instead of piling onto one.
    
      Server applies the ioctl on an O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW fd; inline
      lov_user_md_v1 ABI, no liblustreapi runtime dependency.  ENOTTY/EINVAL
      maps to "not on a layout-capable fs" (silent); EPERM/EACCES to "perm
      denied" (one WARN, latch conn->hpn->layout_set_declined, skip future
      calls on the same conn).
    
      Client decision lives in maybe_apply_lustre_layout() at the top of
      sftp_parallel_upload_dir; gates on parallel mode, server capability,
      hpn-fs-info reporting fs_type=lustre, current stripe < desired, and
      HPNLustreStripeCount != 0.  Success path emits one INFO log naming the
      path and before/after stripe.  Transfer never aborts on a layout
      failure.
    
      Generic extension name reserves room for GPFS/BeeGFS backends with the
      same wire shape in a future revision."

