commit 2ee792910f2391617434470c76bf2ce681987b29
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri May 29 15:49:01 2026 -0400

    sftp: remove the 50 GiB CHUNK_HASH_MAX_FILE_SIZE cap
    
      Sparse-skip + heartbeats now cover the two failure modes the cap was
      meant to defend against: fully-allocated huge files short-circuit via
      the hpn-check-file sentinel (no hashing at all), and long server-side
      hashes refresh the watchdog via heartbeats (no kill-mid-hash).  The
      natural protocol structural cap CHUNK_HASH_MAX_RANGES_PER_REQUEST
      (65536) remains; at 64 MiB chunks it caps single-request chunked
      resume at 4 TiB, which is well above realistic SFTP file sizes.  The
      existing tunables docstring is updated to note that this cap exists
      primarily to bound server-side allocation per request.

