commit 7541b2ff15beb8f5e05fcd02752523371338fd2a
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun May 24 23:11:59 2026 -0400

    Documentation about parallel workers and notices about respawning.
    
    We hadn't included documentatiion about the -j option before. I
    also wanted to give users a notice if there were a lot of respawns
    as this indicates that they requested too many workers. What ends up
    happenin in that case is that a reasonable numbver of worker end up
    doing most of the work and the excess workers are underutilized.
    This end sup with them getting reaped and respawned over and over again.
    
    We tried to deal with this with dynamica allocation but that
    was difficult to implement and overly fragile. So now we just tell
    users to cool their jets.

