commit ab4e4a2c02c40786afff2907eb349cfe7c14428b
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun May 24 11:31:07 2026 -0400

    sftp-hpn-server: document bundle handle lifecycle and invariants
    
      struct hpn_bundle_state has two distinct lifecycles (UPLOAD vs
      FETCH) plus four death paths converging on bundle_state_free.
      Previously the struct had a one-line comment per field; a maintainer
      adding a new entry point had to reverse-engineer the flow from the
      handler functions and the cap-accounting code.
    
      Added a docstring at the struct that lays out:
        - Both lifecycle flows side by side, with the actual entry-point
          functions named (process_hpn_bundle_open / _fetch, the
          sftp_hpn_server_bundle_read / write / close handlers).
        - All four death paths (normal close, fetch-fail, open-fail,
          process exit) and how they converge on bundle_state_free.
        - Ownership invariants — local pointer owns until handle_new_bundle,
          then the handle table owns it; caller MUST NULL the local pointer
          to avoid double-free in the fail label.
        - Memory accounting invariants — bundle_total_bytes is the sum of
          accum_cap across live states, touched only by bundle_state_reserve
          and bundle_state_free.  Any other code path touching accum_cap
          would break the cap enforcement.

commit ed8772b40baccb4d79cb550cfa18ba19f39a35a3
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun May 24 11:26:48 2026 -0400

    sftp-parallel: document worker state lattice (no behaviour change)
    
      The struct sftp_worker carried four interacting fields — health,
      doomed, exited, exited_voluntary — with one-line comments per field
      that didn't show how they relate.  After mapping the semantics:
      these aren't redundant flags, they encode three orthogonal state
      machines (liveness classification, doom-action progression, exit
      lifecycle).  Collapsing to one enum would lose information.
    
      Added a state-lattice docstring on the struct that explicitly lists
      each machine, the valid combinations of states across them, and the
      one brief mutex-protected race window where (DEAD, ¬doomed, ¬exited)
      transiently holds.  Each flag is now tagged (A) / (B) / (C) showing
      which machine it belongs to.
    
      Comment-only change; build clean.

