         (symlinks without -L, non-regular files) left alone. parallel_flush
         surfaces walker_failures_aggregate with a TRANSFER INCOMPLETE
         message. New sticky session_had_failure flag in sftp.c bridges
         interactive mode (where parse_dispatch_command swallows per-command
         errors) so any data-loss event forces non-zero process exit.
    
      3. Abort FD-close: sftp_parallel_abort now closes each worker's SSH
         fd_in/fd_out so blocked get_msg/send_msg returns immediately.
         Ctrl+C to process exit measured at ~10 ms; previously bounded by
         server timeout or RPC completion.

commit ef978d37ff48d930680b0feab5e8586b56b89542
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sat May 23 21:29:26 2026 -0400

    Four correctness fixes:
    
      1. Server-side bundle accumulator caps in sftp-server-hpn.c — per-bundle
         64 MiB and total-across-handles 1.5 GiB, overridable via
         HPN_BUNDLE_MAX_BYTES / HPN_BUNDLE_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES. Stops a buggy or
         malicious client from OOM-ing the server.
    
