commit 18db0784b2f0e98bf07c19020e0b9ab396a25c3c
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri May 22 18:30:12 2026 -0400

    sftp-parallel: fs-info-derived range-split threshold + diagnostics
    
      The range-split threshold is now derived from the Lustre/GPFS stripe
      geometry returned by hpn-fs-info instead of a single 64 MiB constant:
    
          range_split_min = stripe_size × stripe_count × MULTIPLIER × num_workers
    
      Per-fs multipliers (LUSTRE=32 empirical, GPFS=4 placeholder,
      DEFAULT=4 conservative); HPN_STRIPE_MULTIPLIER and the existing
      HPN_RANGE_SPLIT_MIN_MB are honored as overrides.  Files below the
      static 64 MiB floor short-circuit before any fs-info RTT.
    
      Server-side fs-info now walks the path to the first existing
      ancestor before statfs/statvfs/lustre_get_stripe — the client
      typically asks about the upload target before it has been created,
      which previously made fs-info return fs_type=unknown and zeros.
      The old code masked this by falling back to plain alignment;
      the new threshold formula made it visible as a ~3x slowdown.
    
      Visibility: once-per-orchestrator logit() shows the chosen
      threshold and which path (env / formula / floor / fs); per-file
      debug() shows the picked chunk size; per-bundle stderr line shows
      worker / files / bytes / ms / MiBps; optional per-worker stats CSV
      via HPN_WORKER_STATS_CSV; HPN_MAX_AUTH_CONCURRENT lets operators
      cap simultaneous worker handshakes; warning if HPN_USE_BUNDLE is
      set without -j.

commit e7707ad0fd6e490471c882a2dbd70cf8012ef9ab
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri May 22 11:08:33 2026 -0400

    sftp-parallel/client: pipeline bundle WRITEs and add instrumentation
    
      The bundle write path was sending one SSH_FXP_WRITE per 32 KiB libarchive
      block and blocking on STATUS for each — replacing per-file RTT overhead
      with per-block RTT overhead, which is worse than not bundling at all.
      Measured ~0.57 MiB/s per worker against juliet:20003.
    
      bundle_archive_write_cb now sends WRITEs without waiting; STATUS replies
      queue in the SSH channel and are drained in one batch before
      SSH_FXP_CLOSE. libarchive block size bumped from 32 KiB to 128 KiB
      (matches DEFAULT_TRANSFER_BUFLEN, under SFTP_MAX_MSG_LENGTH). Cleanup
      path drains any in-flight STATUSes; if the drain itself fails the conn
      is marked dead so a half-synced channel isn't reused.

