commit 2d622b0ff121d21d601459691c803a19f5833642
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu May 21 23:54:07 2026 -0400

      sftp-parallel: Phase 5 small-file bundling via libarchive
    
      New SFTP extension hpn-bundle@hpnssh.org packs a batch of small files
      into a tar (ustar) stream delivered through one OPEN/WRITE*N/CLOSE on a
      bundle handle, eliminating per-file open/close RTTs that limit Phase 4
      pipelining on high-RTT links. Composes with parallel streams: each
      worker dispatches its own bundles over its own connection.
    
      Opt-in via HPN_USE_BUNDLE=1; target bundle size 4 MiB (override via
      HPN_BUNDLE_TARGET_BYTES). Server advert and client capability check
      gate the path; otherwise the worker falls back to the Phase 4
      pipelined-batch path. libarchive integration is configure-time
      optional (WITH_LIBARCHIVE) — without it the client stub returns -1
      and the server omits the extension advert.

commit 4e0be9e4de8d8e6f554a4f90f946f9dcc630465c
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu May 21 15:10:29 2026 -0400

    sftp-parallel: bytes-based watchdog + non-stripe range-split fallback + interactive defer/wait
    
      Bytes-based progress signal in the watchdog.  Tracks (bytes_total +
      live_bytes) per worker each tick; silence is measured against the last
      tick that saw progress, not against last_completion_ns.  Removes false
      DEAD declarations on long-running whole-file uploads where one unit may
      take longer than STALL_THRESHOLD_SEC but live_bytes is climbing.
    
      Range-split fallback for non-stripe filesystems (ext4/xfs/etc).
      maybe_submit_upload no longer bails to whole-file when stripe info is
      unavailable; instead uses plain file_size/num_ranges chunks (no stripe
      alignment).  Validated on juliet/ext4: -j 2 ≈ 30% over single-stream;
      higher -j adds variance.  Lustre/GPFS path unchanged.
    
      Interactive defer/wait commands.  defer on/off toggles deferred submit
      mode at runtime (same flag batch mode sets automatically); wait drains
      the queue synchronously.  defer off implicitly flushes before turning
      off so successive non-deferred commands work as expected.

