commit 1f0d513b186b3b2957c7a9c27186b99090d7a497
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Mon May 18 23:02:18 2026 -0400

    sftp: non-fatal protocol violations with two-strikes policy
    
      Replace 10 protocol-level fatal()s in sftp-client.c with
      sftp_hpn_set_protocol_violation + graceful return. The connection is
      marked dead so no further I/O happens on it.
    
      Worker policy (sftp-parallel.c): one violation kills just that worker
      and respawns; two in the same hpnsftp lifetime fatal()s. Fixed count
      because a healthy server produces zero — SSH MAC catches in-channel
      tampering below this layer. Motivated by NIC bit-flip bugs on long
      multi-worker transfers.
    
      Control policy (sftp.c): any control-connection violation fatal()s
      immediately, both in interactive_loop and at the three pre-loop
      dispatch sites. Post-wait summary in process_get/put logs a warning
      when a worker violation occurred (transfer recovered via respawn).
    
      sftp_download / sftp_crossload switch-default drains the in-flight
      TAILQ inline so the outer loop exits without an extra dead-conn
      get_msg(). handle_dest_replies leaves *nreqsp > 0 on this path;
      callers must check *write_errorp.

