commit 9fe952e260c87fa48d8391c7f45e98c1bd502eb3
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu May 7 12:31:47 2026 -0400

    Phase 2: respawn ceiling and pending-respawn safeguards
    
    Add a hard ceiling on worker respawns: abort the transfer when total
    lifetime respawns exceed RESPAWN_MULTIPLIER (2) * num_streams. This
    provides a fast exit on sustained connection failures rather than
    grinding through MAX_RETRIES on every queued unit. The multiplier is
    a named define to make the policy explicit and easy to adjust.
    
    Fix a race where the all-workers-gone abort fired prematurely while
    replacement SSH handshakes were still in progress. A pending_respawns
    counter, incremented before pthread_create and decremented in
    respawn_worker_thread, ensures the abort only triggers when no
    recovery is possible.
    
    Wire up reconnect_count, which was tracked in worker stats but never
    incremented. It now reflects actual respawn events and is useful as a
    diagnostic signal alongside units_failed and protocol_violations.

commit e0addd31f231db8d7f80c70b449a297e9ca702b5
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu May 7 11:17:30 2026 -0400

    Phase 2: convert protocol fatal()s to conn->dead with violation flag
    
    Replace fatal() calls for SFTP protocol violations (request ID mismatch,
    unexpected packet type) in get_status, get_handle, get_decode_stat, and
    get_decode_statvfs with error returns that set conn->hpn->dead.
    
    A new protocol_violation flag on struct sftp_hpn_conn distinguishes these
    events from plain connection drops. In parallel mode the worker thread
    checks this flag before the retry logic: violations are counted as hard
    failures and trigger an immediate sftp_parallel_abort() rather than
    requeueing the unit. A fresh connection to a MITM would repeat the same
    violation, so retrying provides no benefit.
    
    All violation sites log at error() level with "possible MITM or server
    protocol corruption" to ensure the event is visible in logs. The count
    is tracked in sftp_parallel_stats.protocol_violations for post-mortem
    inspection. reconnect_count on replacement workers is now incremented
    so the stat is useful as a diagnostic signal.

commit 7281fb5971039728747dca0ffef98fa13f1db773
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu May 7 11:17:00 2026 -0400

    Phase 2: stall detection and worker respawning
    
    Add two new fields to struct sftp_worker (exited_voluntary, doomed) to
    distinguish voluntary exits (EXIT_WORKER sentinel) from connection deaths,
    and to prevent double-SIGTERM on successive watchdog ticks.
    
    When watchdog_check_workers classifies a worker as DEAD it now sends
    SIGTERM to the SSH child process so any blocking I/O unblocks immediately,
    then sets w->doomed. The reporter's reap loop joins exited workers and
    spawns replacements in detached threads (so the SSH handshake does not
    block the 200ms progress ticks) for all non-voluntary exits.
    
    A pending_respawns counter on the orchestrator prevents the all-workers-gone
    abort from firing prematurely while replacement SSH handshakes are in
    progress. The abort fires only when num_workers == 0 and
    pending_respawns == 0 simultaneously with pending work remaining.
    
    Replaces the Phase 1 behaviour of aborting the entire transfer on any
    worker death.

