commit 06cffb0e380c146edbd00e9390e4fa6cd7edd6a4
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Mon May 4 16:20:44 2026 -0400

    firing up 10 or more workers at a time hit the MaxStartups limit.
    
    Unless speicifcally configued to accept for than 10 startups at a time
    sshd processes have a random chance of killing some of the inbound
    connections. This is to prevent DOS attacks. So we need to stagger the
    number of workers started at once. We do it in batchs of 8 to keep it
    below the threshhold.
    
    The user is told which batch of workers is connecting during the process.

