commit 186b0e18861b4d7b2f9c503b8da6f29926eac91b
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun May 3 18:21:47 2026 -0400

      sftp-parallel: recursive transfers via Approach B walker
    
      Replace the synchronous recursive fallback with parallel_{upload,download}_dir,
      which descends the source tree on the control connection (mkdir, readdir)
      and submits regular files to the orchestrator's worker pool as it goes.
      Workers transfer the queued files concurrently while the walker continues
      descending; the caller waits for the queue to drain after the walk
      completes.
    
    Note: This could bottleneck on deep directories. Pipelining the
    directory reads may be important. Look at the readdir logic for this.

