commit ac6d4637a62c65215ae8b4712e6f0b1f5403f68b
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sun May 3 16:52:20 2026 -0400

       sftp: wire -j N flag for parallel-streams transfers
    
       Add the -j parallel_streams flag to hpnsftp and dispatch non-recursive
       put/get to the parallel-streams orchestrator when N > 1. Single-stream
       mode (-j 1, default) is unchanged.
    
       When N > 1, the main connection (conn) handles metadata and the
       orchestrator's N workers handle data transfers. process_put and
       process_get submit each globbed file to the orchestrator instead of
       calling sftp_upload/sftp_download synchronously, then wait on the
       batch to drain before returning.
    
       Recursive transfers, hpnscp parallel support, and pass-through of
       -i/-F/-o to the parallel master are deferred to follow-up steps.
    
       Failure path: if the ControlMaster cannot authenticate (e.g. user
       lacks ssh-agent or pubkey for the host), warn and fall back to
       single-stream mode rather than erroring out. Direct mode (-D) is
       incompatible with -j > 1 (no remote ssh to spawn a master with).

