commit a58ccf860a6c03813f636393fbfe0ad410dd1fdc
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri Apr 24 13:31:50 2026 -0400

    Added regression tests. Fixed an issue where a larger file on the
    remote would end up overwriting the local (and vice versa) and
    added a verified get function for hpnsftp.
    
    The regression tests led to the rest of the changes here.
    
    1) Try to overwrite a larger file is currently causes no
    transfer to take place. I'm not sure if I want to maintain this.
    The issue is that in the case of a failed transfer we expect the
    target to be smaller. Not larger. However, if the idea is to
    keep conformity between the two files then we do want to overwrite.
    
    2) I realized that I had implemented a reputv function in sftp
    but not one to get the files. Whoops.

