commit 5bb680063a43876d9908983a1dc08bee21dccf38
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Fri Apr 24 10:53:47 2026 -0400

    Append directly to target file instead of using tmp file
    when we are using the resume function.
    
    The tmp file thing was a kludge because I couldn't figure out
    how to append correctly to the target file. This fixes that and
    really removes a lot of complexity. Additionally, I put in some
    exception handling when the user is connecting to a system that
    uses the old blake512b hash. We do not gracefully fallback to that
    hash because a) This is for legacy scp which is deprecated and b)
    I don't think many people were using it so it's not a huge problem
    to remove that support and c) having that fallback is a lot of added
    complexity we don't need.

