commit db99bbd9b4f346b20e19c222036aa9f9b51c677c
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Mon Apr 13 18:09:46 2026 -0400

    Allow user defined receive buffer limits.
    
    This is a new server/client option to let users determine
    how much memory they are willing to use for their sessions.
    The default is 128MB (which is what it currently is). They
    can also use 'high' which corresponds to 256MB or max which
    is 512MB. Initial tests show this makes a big difference at
    higher RTTs. Needs more validation though.

