    it is cleared with pthread_attr_destroy. This changes does that
    post thread creation.

commit 9689ad8767998a0ffc7e7558c89bd1e8dc4f85fb
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Apr 8 11:27:34 2026 -0400

        Clear up minor leak when using NONEMAC.
    
        Using NONEMAC requires NONE. In sshconnect2.c's ssh_userauth()
        we populate the kex proposal entries first with none_cipher and the
        normal range of MACs and then, if none_enabled is true we
        populate it *again* with none_cipher and none_mac. Which means
        we are potentially leaking information because we use xstrdup
        to fill the proposal string. The fix is freeing the existing
        proposal before we repopulate it.

